The method returns null if no rows match. Here's how to handle it:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Load some data into the table
await table.loadData("./data.csv");
// Try to get first row with non-existent category
const firstRow = await table.getFirstRow({
  conditions: "category = 'NonExistent'"
});
if (!firstRow) {
  console.log("No rows found matching the condition.");
}
// Close everything
await sdb.done();
```

Filter rows inside the function before mapping:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Load data into the table
await table.loadData("./data.csv");
// Update rows: only modify rows where status is 'pending'
await table.updateWithJS((rows) => {
  return rows.map((d) => {
    if (d.status === "pending") {
      return { ...d, status: "processed" };
    }
    return d;
  });
});
// Log the first rows
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

