Using `setTypes` will replace any existing table with the new schema. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// Create a table and add some data
const table = sdb.newTable("existingTable");
await table.loadData("./data.csv");
// Now set types, which will replace the existing table
await table.setTypes({
  id: "integer",
  name: "string"
});
// The old data is replaced with the new schema
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

