You can specify the exact column(s) to use for the join. Here's an example:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// Create two tables
const tableA = sdb.newTable("tableA");
const tableB = sdb.newTable("tableB");
// Load data into both tables
await tableA.loadData("./dataA.csv");
await tableB.loadData("./dataB.csv");
// Perform a join using 'id' as the common column
await tableA.join(tableB, {
  commonColumn: "id"
});
// Log the joined results
await tableA.logTable();
// Close everything
await sdb.done();
```
This example specifies 'id' as the common column for joining.

