The cache is invalidated automatically when the function body changes, so the new function will be executed on the next call.
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();

// First run with initial function
await table.cache(async () => {
  await table.loadData("items.csv");
  await table.summarize({
    values: "price",
    categories: "department",
    summaries: ["min", "max", "mean"],
  });
});

// Later, modify the function (e.g., add a new summary)
await table.cache(async () => {
  await table.loadData("items.csv");
  await table.summarize({
    values: "price",
    categories: "department",
    summaries: ["min", "max", "mean", "sum"],
  });
}); // Cache will refresh because function changed

// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

