You can use the `test` option to add a validation step. Here's how:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// Load some data
await table.loadArray([{ text: "Hello" }, { text: "World" }]);
// Use aiRowByRow with a test function
await table.aiRowByRow(
  "text",
  "sentiment",
  "What is the sentiment of this text?",
  {
    test: (dataPoint: unknown) => {
      if (typeof dataPoint !== "string") {
        throw new Error("Invalid response: Not a string");
      }
    },
  },
);
// Log the table to see the results
await table.logTable();
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```
The `test` function will be called for each AI response. If it throws an error, the request will be considered failed.

