```

Resources may not be freed properly. Here's why you should always call it:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// Always include done() to clean up
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
await sdb.done(); // Proper cleanup
```

Here's how you can retrieve boolean values from a specific column:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
// We start a SimpleDB instance
const sdb = new SimpleDB();
// We create a new table
const table = sdb.newTable();
// We load data from a file
await table.loadData("./my-data.csv");
// We get all values from the 'is_active' column
const is_active_values = await table.getValues("is_active");
console.log(is_active_values); // e.g., [true, false, true]
// We close everything
await sdb.done();
```

You can specify the geometry column to validate:
```
import { SimpleDB } from "@nshiab/simple-data-analysis";
